 "text": "Hey there, how are you? You don't need talent to learn. A good rule is to draw your favorite thing, ten times in a row. Pick something simple, like a box, and focus on one part of it each time. The difference is who's doing the work. Your brain is working hard in both cases, but in the first it's thinking about what to say and in the second it' thinking about how to draw. That's fine. Start with stick figures and move on from there.",
